Inkpoint Multi-Licensing Scheme
===============================

Inkpoint is an open source project licensed under a multi-licensing model
designed to protect end-user applications from proprietary commercial wrapping
while maximizing the reuse and adoption of its underlying libraries and engines.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Applications & Presentation Layer: GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All client applications and presentation services located under:
- `apps/desktop/`
- `apps/mobile/` (including `core`, `android`, and `ios`)
- `apps/web/`
- `site/`

are licensed under the GNU General Public License, Version 3.0 (or, at your option,
any later version) as published by the Free Software Foundation.

See the full text in `LICENSE-GPL` or below.

### Apple App Store Exception (for iOS):

As a special exception to the GNU General Public License v3.0, the copyright
holders of Inkpoint give permission to distribute the Inkpoint application
through Apple's App Store under the terms of the Apple App Store Terms of Service,
notwithstanding anything to the contrary in Section 6 of the GNU General Public
License v3.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Core Libraries, Plugins & Utilities: MIT License
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

All core packages, extensions, and integration modules located under:
- `packages/*` (including `editor-core`, `renderer-codemirror`, `editor-ui`,
  `compiler`, `syntax-plugins`, `mdx-component-registry`, `mdx-plugins`,
  `markdown-fidelity`, `file-system`, `i18n`, `ai`, and `shared`)
- `apps/utools/`
- `infra/distribution-worker/`

are licensed under the permissive MIT License. You are free to use, copy, modify,
merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of these libraries
without copyleft restrictions.

See the full text in `LICENSE-MIT` or below.

